REPLACE_ME_WITH_A_YANDEX_OAUTH_TOKEN

# Copy to secrets/yandex-token, replacing the line above and deleting these
# comments -- yandex-trash strips whitespace but not commentary.
#
# Used by `yandex-trash` to list and restore from the Yandex Disk trash. That
# trash is what covers deletions inside the 15-minute window between restic
# snapshots: the sync daemon pushes a delete to the cloud within seconds, and
# the server keeps the file.
#
# rclone cannot do this job. Its yandex backend implements exactly one trash
# operation, CleanUp(), which permanently empties the whole bin -- so the only
# trash capability rclone offers is the one that destroys the safety net.
# Never run `rclone cleanup yandex:`.
#
# To mint a token:
#   1. Register an application at https://oauth.yandex.com/
#   2. Grant scopes: cloud_api:disk.read and cloud_api:disk.write
#   3. Complete the consent flow and copy the access token here
#
# The same token can go into secrets/rclone.conf, so one consent flow covers
# both tools. Tokens are long-lived but do expire; `yandex-trash list` reports
# a rejected token explicitly rather than failing obscurely.
#
# Override at runtime with YANDEX_DISK_TOKEN or YANDEX_DISK_TOKEN_FILE.
